TIKI
// HZM coop [user 2026-09-06, bug-2508] HIGGINS BOW WAKE MESH - the m3l1a run-in (ocean_2026-09-06 item 3).
//
// Retail shipped this wake for the Higgins (main/Pak0.pk3 models/fx/wake.tik, QUAKED fx_water_higginswake)
// and never placed it on m3l1a - zero references in the map script or the entity lump. The MESH stays in
// the retail pak: `path models/fx/wake` + `skelmodel wake.skd` resolves to Pak0 models/fx/wake/wake.skd
// (1 surface named `wake`, 44 verts / 52 tris, parsed 2026-09-06). The CLIP does not: retail's wake.skc is
// SKAN version 11 and SkeletorCacheFileCallback (tiki/tiki_files.cpp:578-592) accepts only versions 13
// and 14, so pointing at it aborted TIKI init and the model never appeared. models/fx/wake/coop_wake.skc
// is that single frame re-encoded as v13 by docs/tools/gen_coop_wake_skc.py, shipped in the mod pk3 in
// the same directory as the retail skd (that is why `path models/fx/wake` stays).
//
// WHY A COPY AND NOT THE RETAIL TIK. Retail's init { server { } } is `classname drivablevehicle` plus
// setsize / seatoffset / gravity 0.6 / vehiclespeed 1200 / canjump, and a tik's server init block runs
// even when a script spawns it as a script_model (TRAPS, TIKI traps, bug-2244). A wake that is a drivable
// vehicle with gravity would sink off the hull and offer the player a seat. This copy is the
// coop_bloodcloud carrier pattern: effectentity, notsolid, and NO +dontdraw - the mesh IS the effect.
//
// SHADER. Retail `wake` (Pak0 scripts/wake.shader) multiplies in `$lightmap` as its last stage, which is
// meaningless on an entity (no lightmap; on gl2 it binds the white image, on gl1 it is undefined). The
// surface points at `coop_wake` in scripts/zz_coop_wake.shader instead - retail's block minus that stage,
// keeping `deformvertexes wave` (a TIKI mesh writes real normals, tr_model.cpp:1664, so the wave deform
// works on it, GPU path) and the two scrolling oceandday layers. One name, one coop file (TRAPS T6).
//
// PLACEMENT (script side, level.coop_wakeOn). The clip POSES THE MESH ABOVE ITS ORIGIN: frame bounds
// z 74.7..143.9 in bone space = +39..+75 u at this scale (wake.skd posed through its rot channel lands
// exactly on those bounds - see the generator). So it is bound at HULL z, not at the water: the pivot
// rests at -524 during the ride, coop_wakeLift -53 puts the origin at about -577, and the +39..+75 band
// straddles the -520 surface. Forward is model -X (the 209 u lobe); the 375 u +X lobe trails. Extents
// at scale 0.52: x -209..+375, y -140..+143 - Higgins sized; the hull is 610 u long. A north-bound
// hull therefore takes yaw 270 (model -X = world +Y).
setup
{
	scale 0.52
	path models/fx/wake
	skelmodel wake.skd
	surface wake shader coop_wake
}

init
{
	server
	{
		classname effectentity
		notsolid
	}
}

animations
{
	// Both point at the one-frame v13 clip beside the retail skd (header). `start` exists so a caller's
	// `anim start` is a real animation. [user 2026-09-06, bug-2508]
	idle  coop_wake.skc
	start coop_wake.skc
}
